<title>USA: Bumpers willing to back 2002 for open power market.</title>
<headline>Bumpers willing to back 2002 for open power market.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Sen. Dale Bumpers said Wednesday he would be willing to support a deadline in mid-2002 instead of 2003 for all states to be required to open their power markets to competition.</p>
<p>The Arkansas Democrat last month introduced legislation that would make states break up local utility monopolies and give all consumers freedom to choose their power suppliers by the end of 2003.</p>
<p>Similar legislation being pushed in the House calls for an open market by the end of 2000.</p>
<p>&quot;I'd be willing to meet them half way,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
